a critical inquiry on the rise of the concept of \u201cculture\u201d and of its prefixations (multi, inter, cross, trans), contrasting it with categories such as \u201cglobal(ized),\u201d \u201cplanetary,\u201d \u201cuniversal,\u201d \u201ccosmopolitics.\u201d We\u2019ll articulate literary theory with anthropology, experimental psychology with political theory, or ethics with biology (\u201canimal culture\u201d now forming a legitimate category). We\u2019ll additionally study some cases of transcultural circulations in the human context (science, literature and the arts), especially between Europe, Asia, and the Caribbean.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2026SP", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2923, "crseId": 366995, "crseOfferNbr": 2, "subject": "ROMS", "catalogNbr": "4944", "titleShort": "Digital Biopolitics", "titleLong": "Digital Biopolitics", "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "ALC-AS", "descr": "AS-Arts, Literat, and Culture", "descrformal": "AS-Arts, Literature, and Culture", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}], "crseAttrValueGroups": [{"attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "crseAttrValues": "(ALC-AS)"}], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 1231, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr":